WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.860
Z.ai just showed how far post-training alone can push a fixed base model into serious coding and cyber agent territory. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 142. The same 743-753 billion parameter base that powered GLM 5.2 now delivers 28.3 on terminal bench 3.0 after expanded post-training. Deep-swee version 1.1 rose from 46.2

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:53.300
to 66.9. Automation bench move from 26.2 to 48.2. Agents last exam CLI climbed from 23.8 to 28.5. On the private z.ai code bench, the new model reaches 34.5% at maximum reasoning effort while using roughly 75,000 output tokens per task.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:01:23.280
CyberGym accuracy increased from 77.2% to 84.5%. Exploit bench jumped from 24.4% to 54.4%. ExploitGym completed 105 tasks in a 2-hour budget and 130 tasks in 6 hours. The model already surfaced a potentially serious vulnerability in cursor, prompting z.ai to add trusted access controls and post-pone open weights plus gems.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:36.360
Interprise users can now run autonomous coding agents that plan, implement, test, and verify multi-date tasks inside the z-code environment on macOS, Windows or Linux.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:50.440
Three explicit reasoning effort levels must be chosen because thinking can no longer be disabled. Open-weight labs continue narrowing the gap with closed frontier systems through targeted post-training rather than new pre-training runs.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:02:06.120
Simon Willison shared a direct link to LMStudio's 17 Gigabyte Q4KM quantized build of the corrected Quinn 3.827b model. The build runs locally and resolves earlier version number confusion in community discussion.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:18.460
Builders working with local inference can test the model immediately through LMStudio. Anthropic published an FAQ confirming watermarking will be added to meet the EU AI Act code of practice.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:35.660
The method adds no tokens, hidden characters or quality degradation and cannot be traced to any individual user or conversation. Developers using clawed outputs in regulated environments gain a compliance path that leaves existing prompts, pricing, and output behavior unchanged.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:46.840
The company also released its second detailed risk report under the responsible scaling policy. The redacted PDF is now public and covers system risks and preparedness measures.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:59.460
NEC launched what it describes as the first all AI department staffed by 17 autonomous agents. The setup targets internal operations without human staff in the loop for routine tasks.

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:07.900
Organizations experimenting with fully agentic teams now have a concrete enterprise example to study for scaling patterns and failure modes.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:15.780
Reports highlight Gemini 3.7 Flash as a potential benchmarking environment for autonomous agents operating in crypto markets.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:29.120
The models speed and cost profile make it attractive for high frequency tool using agent loops. Developers building financial or on-tane agents can use the flash tier to prototype before moving to higher capability variance.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:42.900
A 150 million parameter BDHCQ system updates recurrent memory from in-context demonstrations and solves queries through iterative latent space computation without verbalizing intermediate steps.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:04:01.760
It reaches 29.5% pass at 2 on ARC AGI-1 at roughly 0.00070 dollars per task. Researchers exploring memory augmented or non-verbal reasoning architectures can examine the approach for tasks where token level chain of thought is undesirable.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:12.820
A 21 billion parameter transformer was created by compiling dooms rendering algorithm directly into weights using a custom computation graph compiler with no training involved.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:27.260
The resulting hugging face checkpoint accepts scene prompts and outputs pixel drawing commands that produce the E1M1 frame after 53,747 generated tokens from a 3614 token prompt.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:49.000
One frame takes approximately 40 minutes on a B200 GPU. The open source on-co-thresh Python package plus web dashboard come to sensitivity, specificity, PPV, NPV, decision curve net benefit and bootstrap intervals at user specified clinical thresholds for continuous oncology model outputs.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:05:05.380
It targets tasks such as CHI-67 or PDL-1 scoring where global metrics like AUC are insufficient. Pathologists and model developers working with threshold-based decisions can run the library locally via Docker without cloud dependencies.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:25.620
Okay, let's pop the hood on post-training scaling without new pre-training. Everyone treats post-training as a simple add more RL step. Yet the engineering reality is a carefully staged expansion of environments, task diversity and reinforcement learning compute that can unlock capabilities the base model never saw in pre-training.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:41.540
The process begins by reusing the identical foundation weights and then progressively exposing the model to longer horizon scenarios such as full code bases, multi-day engineering jobs, and vulnerability discovery chains while keeping the parameter count fixed.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:53.400
Each added environment increases the density of useful gradients but also raises the risk that capabilities such as exploitation chain construction emerge faster than safety evaluations can track.

00:05:53.960 --> 00:06:07.260
In GLM 5.3's case, the same base moved from 4.6 to 28.3 on terminal bench and from 24.4 to 54.4 on exploit bench solely through this scaling.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:20.160
The practical trade-off is that teams gain substantial capability without another multi-hundred million dollar pre-training run. Yet they inherit the same difficult access control problem that closed labs already face.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:33.140
Use this route when your base model already covers the domain and you can afford extensive environment engineering. Fall back to fresh pre-training only when the target capability lies outside the current weight distribution.

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:43.220
The approach also forces changes in how applications call the model since reasoning effort must now be explicitly chosen and thinking cannot be turned off.

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:57.380
Load LM Studio's Q4KM build of QN 3.827B locally and compare its coding throughput against your current 7-13B models on a representative SWE bench subset.

00:06:57.380 --> 00:07:07.620
Review Anthropics redacted risk report PDF to see how one lab structures capability evaluations ahead of any EU mandated water marking rollout.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:20.720
Clone the BDH-CQ repository once released and test the 150M recurrent latent setup on a small ARC-AGI subset to measure the claimed cost accuracy improvement.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:31.300
Run the Onco Thresh dashboard on your own oncology model outputs to generate threshold specific calibration and net benefit curves before the next clinical review.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:40.740
Experiment with Z-Codes goal tasks on the GLM coding plan to observe how the new reasoning effort controls affect long horizon agent workflows.

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:48.940
Z.AI plans to release GLM 5.3 weights roughly two weeks after launch once safety hardening completes.

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:56.320
Staged GLM 5.3 API access is expected after the current trusted access controls are validated.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:08:05.280
